/E (An ongoing collaboration exploring the environmental affordances of re-making led by Molly Volanth Hall, Jade French, and Diana Cristina Proenza. Inspired by modernist makers like Mina Loy, Richard Bruce Nugent, the Baroness Elsa von Freytag-Loringhoven, Kurt Schwitters, and Virginia Woolf, these Modernism and Environment SIG-sponsored workshops bring participants together to explore a shared impulse towards remediation, reuse, and recycling in the literary and artistic avant-garde of modernism, recovering an ethic of sustainability at the heart of modernist aesthetics and histories, though not always expressed in directly environmental terms. )
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
